/-!
# Checked tables for the native Golay comparison

The saved 55-bit wedge columns are decoded on upper triangular pairs. A second
encoding packs those same pairs into 121 bits so XOR checks can reuse the
proved binary decoder. The exterior tables are checked against the alternating
products of the actual saved eleven-dimensional generator columns. The native
row-action check includes the exact constant-word corrections.

Witnesses: `KernelAbsolute/source/native-data.json`, obtained from the native
Golay rows and permutations, not an external representation. Source context:
James (1973), pp.57–111; GM02 Proposition 5.1, manuscript p.17.
-/

